    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0302" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1262"/>

                <head>No. 848.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, concerning the fine imposed by the customs
                    authorities at San Diego, California, upon the Mexican vessel <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Monserrat</hi>, on account of a defect in her papers,
                    stated to have been duly authenticated, but accidentally lost by the capsizing
                    of a small boat to which they had been transferred.</p>
                <p>In reply I desire to say that a copy of your note has been sent to the Secretary
                    of the Treasury for the consideration of his Department.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
